 "notes": [
  "Ward numbering: all tables use the old ward numbers 168-180 (Adyar zone); the Chairman/Zonal Officer rows and the map pages (pp. 679, 692, 698, 702, 709) use the new numbers 170-182. Map ward labels are consistently offset (map ward = table ward + 2 in most legends). Ward values below are copied from the tables as printed.",
  "Zonal office address/phone not given in this appendix.",
  "Water stagnation, heavy rain (p. 693): heading 'only overflow of Adyar river' with no table; the untitled street/pump/disposal table on p. 695 (4 rows, 'inundation seen') is recorded under inundation_streets, one entry per street. Depth and days-to-drain not given. Mild rain table says 'Nill'.",
  "Sewer-block rows (rain=sewer_block) also list manhole counts (not stored). Ward 176 lists 3 counts (3,2,3) for only 2 streets.",
  "Relief centres: text says 16 centres / capacity 5700, but the table has 18 rows. Column order in the PDF is Drinking water, Toilets, Cooking facilities (all 'Yes, Yes, No' except row 13 'Yes, Yes, Yes'). Contacts are recorded per row as printed (each row carries only part of the per-ward Evacuation/Food/Relief Materials/Sanitation contact block); 'responsibility' added to each contact.",
  "Relief centre row 3 (ward 168) name cell reads 'Chennai Higher Secondary School Little Mount Annai Velankanni school, Hospital road Govt ITI' - likely three centres in one cell (CHS Little Mount, Annai Velankanni school, Govt ITI) sharing capacity 750; kept verbatim as one entry.",
  "Relief centre rows 5 & 6 (ward 170) share one merged capacity cell '250'; recorded as 250 on both. Row 5 responsibility for both contacts is 'Sanitation, Medicine & Drinking water'; row 6 responsibility cell reads 'Sanitary Inspector'. Rows 8-9 are labelled ward '170 - Kotturpuram' though the streets column says 'Adyar'. Row 13 ward printed '176176' (recorded as 176).",
  "Relief-centre map legend (p. 702, new ward numbers) lists 22 shelters R1-R22 including several not in the table: CHS Little mount (R1), Govt ITI (R4), Teachers Training Institute (R6), St.Francis Xavier school, Little Mount (R8), CHS Annasalai (R9), Gandhimandapam (R11), Rajaji Mandapam (R12), ABCD Park stadium (R13), CMS - NS Garden (R15), J.J Kalyanamandapam (Community Centre) (R16), Multipurpose hall - Ambedkar nagar 18th cross street (R19). Not added to relief_centres (no capacity/contacts; different ward numbering). The same map lists 18 'streets/areas people to be shifted' S1-S18.",
  "Streets that require evacuation: table says '168 - 180 Nil' (no evacuation done in 2017). Evacuation-area map p. 709 lists 28 areas E1-E28 (new ward numbers) which correspond to the boat/NDRF locations, not to an evacuation table.",
  "Lighting row for wards '179,180' (phone 9445191468) has no Sl. No. and a blank designation; designation left null.",
  "Boat table is titled 'For 2018' (none used in NEM 2017); single shared contact cell for all rows. Mid-word line wraps in the 'Boats stationed location' column re-joined (e.g. 'Muru/gunagar' -> 'Murugunagar').",
  "Park 'location' field holds the 'Name Of Ward' column. Ward 178 lines 'CSIR Road,' and 'Ticel park Taramani, Chennai-113' joined as one park (total then matches the stated 84 parks). Some park rows are road names (e.g. 'Velachery Main Road', 'Rajiv gandhi road') as printed.",
